Facebook

04:03.980 --> 04:08.940
From VOA learning English, this is the technology report

04:09.660 --> 04:17.140
High-tech companies are developing the next generation of products that will help us drive cars

04:17.460 --> 04:19.460
do our shopping and

04:20.140 --> 04:25.740
even care for our children the technology company Intel

04:26.340 --> 04:33.220
Recently held a demonstration of some of its new devices in San Francisco

04:34.500 --> 04:38.780
One device measured how alert a driver was

04:39.900 --> 04:44.900
Sensors connected to the driver's head measured brain activity

04:45.940 --> 04:51.740
Cameras placed on the cars dashboard measured eye movement

04:52.940 --> 04:54.340
Justin Ratner

04:54.340 --> 04:56.740
Works at Intel Labs

04:58.180 --> 05:00.180
He says the devices

05:00.860 --> 05:07.340
Measure how much of the brain is occupied while the person is driving

05:08.540 --> 05:13.580
Devices like these he says will make driving safer

05:14.740 --> 05:23.540
Another experimental Intel technology links cars electronically to help prevent crashes

05:24.340 --> 05:27.140
When the driver of the car in front

05:27.700 --> 05:35.060
Signals a turn or slows down an alert message is sent to the car in back

05:36.100 --> 05:40.940
There was also a demonstration of a virtual computer

05:41.540 --> 05:49.500
The computer was projected onto the table from a controller hidden in a flower pot

05:50.500 --> 05:58.500
Sensors read the movements of the user's hands. So there was no need for a mouse or other

05:59.100 --> 06:01.100
handheld device

06:01.300 --> 06:07.020
This technology could be used in everyday situations

06:07.700 --> 06:09.700
At a market

06:09.700 --> 06:15.860
Sensors and computer chips placed in products could help shoppers

06:16.100 --> 06:18.900
Find the items they want to buy

06:19.900 --> 06:28.900
For example, the technology could help them avoid foods that could cause an allergic reaction

06:29.900 --> 06:36.900
Cameras and sensors are already available to help parents watch their children

06:37.900 --> 06:44.300
In the future, other equipment will monitor a baby's health and mood

06:44.700 --> 06:52.700
And security systems are being improved and simplified with face recognition software

06:53.100 --> 06:57.100
Instead of complicated passwords

06:57.100 --> 06:59.100
For VOA Learning

